On OpenRouter, Claude models now get their real limits and price, and the default no longer runs on guessed limits. One change from your plan: the new default is anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5, not anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6. Neither yoyo nor yoagent 0.25.16 has a preset for sonnet 4.6, so that default would still have been capped at max_tokens = 4096 with the warning firing. Sonnet 5.5 is in OpenRouter's catalog and has a preset. Committed as `7076903c`; fmt, clippy (`-D warnings`), the full cargo test and tests/harness_logic.sh (325/0) all pass.

What changed
• The mapping: a new function in src/providers.rs turns anthropic/claude-opus-4.8 (or the dashed spelling) into the preset id claude-opus-4-8. It returns nothing for ids without the anthropic/ prefix, for an empty id, and for :variant ids like :batch. Those cost half the regular price, so mapping them would show twice the real cost in /cost.
• Where it's used: only the openrouter provider uses it for limits; it copies the window, max_tokens, price and reasoning flag. The id sent to OpenRouter stays exactly as the user typed it.
• Pricing: both price lookups in src/format/cost.rs use the same mapping. Before, anthropic/claude-opus-4.8 missed its preset and was priced at the old $15/$75 Opus rate.
• Probe on the built binary:
  • Before: the default and anthropic/claude-opus-4.8 both printed "no preset is known … 128000-token context window and max_tokens = 4096".
  • After: neither warns (opus-4.8 now gets 1M / 64000).
  • anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6 still warns.
• Tests: the new src/openrouter_preset_tests.rs covers the mapping, the limits, cases that must still warn, the custom provider not mapping, the default, and /cost. I broke the mapping on purpose, one place at a time: each break turned the expected tests red, and each restore turned them green again.
• Existing tests updated on purpose:
  • The default-model test is renamed for the new id.
  • The list of providers whose default runs on guessed limits lost exactly openrouter, which is now required to stay silent.
  • tests/module_size.rs raises the src/format/cost.rs cap from 3640 to 3647.
• Docs: models.md and installation.md both listed an older default (claude-sonnet-4-20250514); both now say sonnet-5.5, and models.md explains the mapping.
• Known-model list: OpenRouter has no known-model list. The dashed entry at src/providers.rs:180 belongs to github, so I left it alone.

Still open (posted on #1037; the first line starts "Scope: openrouter row done = …"):
• OpenRouter lists sonnet-4.6, opus-4.7, opus-4.6, opus-4.5, sonnet-4.5 and opus-4.1, but none has a preset, so they still run on guessed limits and warn. haiku-4.5 does have a preset; I first listed it here by mistake, checked it on the binary, and corrected the comment.
• :batch variants stay on guessed limits until their half price is handled.
• Not verified: whether OpenRouter rejects the old dashed default id. I have no key to test it.
